Description: non-intrusive terminal AI assistant with session-scoped context
 ask is a lightweight command-line query tool designed specifically for
 system administrators and infrastructure engineers who want succinct AI
 guidance without disrupting their terminal workflow.
 .
 Unlike heavyweight interactive AI assistants or terminal UI wrappers, ask
 executes directly in standard shell pipelines, streams direct answers to
 standard output, and exits immediately.
 .
 Context is automatically scoped to the parent shell process (PPID), allowing
 conversational follow-up questions within the same terminal tab without
 cross-contaminating other active shell sessions. Long sessions use
 token-aware auto-compaction to preserve crucial context without arbitrary
 timeouts or extra latency.
